{
    "background_story": "In the depths of the Pacific Ocean, there existed a rare and majestic scyphozoan jellyfish named Sweetkins. Her translucent bell-shaped body glowed with a soft, ethereal light, illuminating the dark waters. Sweetkins was a gentle giant, drifting lazily on the currents, her stinging tentacles waving harmlessly in the water. Despite her fearsome reputation, she was a curious and playful creature, often interacting with the local sea life. Sweetkins had a special bond with a school of sparkling fish, who would dart in and out of her tentacles in a dazzling display of underwater acrobatics. As the seasons passed, Sweetkins became a beloved fixture in the ocean community, her scyphozoan beauty captivating all who encountered her.",
